Task: Locate the anchor function for the state_code field in the console.log object whose action is workspace.commit after filling Workspace Key with project-alpha-2024, selecting Sync Interval 30 seconds, checking Offline Mode, and clicking Apply Workspace. The anchor is the first target-specific value-construction function on the dynamic behavior chain: it appears after routing, workspace action-table resolution, scope-field selection, and input preparation, and its own function body constructs the target workspace state-encoding hash value instead of merely collecting workspace parameters, forwarding control, wrapping a return value, or emitting to the sink. Return exactly one complete JavaScript function and its location in the captured corpus. Do not return a generic utility, event handler, action-table dispatcher, scope resolver, full call chain, or final console sink.

Example value pattern: ^sc_[a-z0-9]{12}$
Observable: {"type": "console", "method": "log", "action": "workspace.commit", "field": "state_code", "format": "^sc_[a-z0-9]{12}$"}

Shortlisted functions:
### eb914a9e8f9c2b03 (v00)
```js
function v00(input = {}) {
  const normalized = normalize00(input);
  const folded = fold00(normalized.rows, normalized.seed);
  const digest = digest00(folded, normalized.label);
  const total = folded.out.reduce((sum, item) => (sum + item) >>> 0, folded.a ^ folded.b);
  const bucket = normalized.rows.map((item, idx) => ({ idx, item, mark: (Number(item) + idx + 0) % 17 }));
  return { index: 0, total, digest, bucket, label: normalized.label };
}
```
### 278fdadac92f9a15 (encodeValue)
```js
function encodeValue(value, salt) {
  const text = String(value || "");
  const out = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < text.length; i += 1) {
    out.push(((text.charCodeAt(i) + salt + i) % 91 + 35).toString(36));
  }
  return out.join(".");
}
```

